A||||14||V8Fiero||Tow Dolly/U-haul ||||5||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||05-31-2001||08:31 PM||||Just wondering if anyone has used the uhaul tow dollys with good results. With any luck here in the next two weeks Im gonna be towing a GT 1400 miles cross country.<P>TIA<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||grinthock||05-31-2001||08:36 PM||||NO!   I tried to use one on my 85 when I first got it, ended up that we couldn't get it on without banging the exhaust or damging the facia, if you goto uhaul they have a list of what cars fit.. They told me I needed the carrier, I said ahh screw it It'll fit, and it didn't..... (Well my dad said he could make it fit!)  What I ended up doing was asking the seller (a friend) to lend me the plates (still valid) so I could get the car home then I mailed the plates back||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||05-31-2001||08:37 PM||||I've used them for everything from fullsize cop cars to VW Bugs. Just don't try to back them up, things get kinda bent!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000003||westtexas||05-31-2001||08:55 PM||||I used a U-Haul dolly to bring a '87 2.5 auto with a blown engine 40 miles. Carried the back end on the dolly. Just used the steering lock to keep the front wheels straight. The hardest part was pushing it up onto the dolly. With the help of a younger, stronger person and several tries at a 10 yard running start we finally aimed right and got it up there. Next time I'll take a fence stretcher. It towed fine at 60 mph and didn't bottom out on anything. Good Luck. Robert||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||05-31-2001||09:10 PM||||i did it last year with a 4cyl auto. did it wrong and towed it forward in neutral. found out later it was wrong but it made it ok. about 150 mls.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WMEBERT||05-31-2001||09:44 PM||||I just towed my 86 GT home last Friday night with a U-Haul tow dolly behind my 96 S10 Blazer. I backed it on the dolly and locked the wheels straight and had NO problems.  It was an easy tow.  Towing the dolly empty was "fun", it bounced all over the place.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000006||MooCow||05-31-2001||09:48 PM||||Can't you use one of the bigger trucks they have and put the Fiero inside??  To me that seems like the easiest way to do it without any damage done to the car.  Am I way off cause I think I am going to do that to bring my car down to Ed Parks if I don't do the head gaskets myself.<P>                             Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000007||V8Fiero||05-31-2001||11:04 PM||||How would you get it in the back of a big truck? Besides that the gas would kill ya. At least me it would.<P>Just got an email back from FieroDave. I saw on his website that he uses a tow dolley. Guess what kind? U-HAUL!. Says it works great.<P>Thanks guys.<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||KissMySSFiero||05-31-2001||11:55 PM||||unless your pullig with your fiero get a trailer.  at least if you get it from uhaul.  if you have a truck get the full trailer.  i believe is actaully cheaper.  because they wont let you take it unless you have lights to go on the back up the trailered car.  when i had to pull my car we did this becuase we didnt have any lights and uhaul wanted too much for them.  i think the 88's you couldnt pull on the dolly.||||reg||1
Z||000009||V8Fiero||06-01-2001||12:03 AM||||Im gonna pull with an aerostar van. Only has a class two hitch. I dont think the van would do very good with towing a complete trailer. Uhaul wanted $170 for the dolley compared to $340 for the trailer. Not cheaper here.<BR><P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||sjp777||06-01-2001||12:09 AM||||If you're only going 10 miles or less, you can probably get away with a dolly, otherwise, get the full trailer. It's not that much more, although you will need a bigger truck<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> 88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||gabriel||06-01-2001||12:37 PM||||My advice is to tell UHAUL to take a friggin hike, & go with Penske.  My cost for a 15ft truck AND the carrier = $115.   UHAUL s**ks!||||reg||1
Z||000012||V8Fiero||06-01-2001||05:35 PM||||No Penske around these parts. Just Uhaul and Ryder. Ryder doesnt even rent the dollys or trailers without the truck.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||rogergarrison||06-01-2001||06:17 PM||||I just bought a used tow dolly. it has steerable wheels, im modifying the tie downs to clear my spoiler. Just spent a day rewiring it for my Lumina minivan. I just needed to make 2 longer ramps to get the bottom cleared. I have 4 speed so plan on towing mine with front up. I got it so I can go to places like Mid Ohio and camp out and still have my car with me. Only cost me $300. my van has a class III hitch.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierodave||06-02-2001||05:49 AM||||You can use a U-haul dolly for any year Fiero and tow it front first with a stick or backwards with an auto!  makes no difference!<P>I do notice on long trips you get better gas mileage towing front first (stick car only)  but, they seem to tow better with the car on backwards!<P>When I was in Ca and I bought all them Fieros out there last November we hauled over 45 of the Fieros from Sacramento to Merced Ca. & delivered 5 of them to customers, hauled 15 to the junk yard & them moved them all to a different storage lot, and with out one bent pipe or a problem at all!!  <P>We bought that dolly from a U-Haul center in Fresno for $650.00  and have since towed over 30 more with the darn thing.  <P>There are taillights on all of the dollys and no extra lights are needed to be put on the car at all. <P>If that u-haul center says you need them them BUNK! they just want to <BR>rent you some lights is all!<P>I wore out the first set of straps  we hauled so many on the dolly!!!!<P>I pulled a 87 GT back from Ca behind a loaded 26foot truck on that same dolly!  <BR>Anyone that says you can't haul with one or you need a trailer is smokin to much stuff!!!  use the u-haul dolly! load it backwards and forget about what others are saying.  <P>I just pulled a 85 GT back from minn two weeks ago and a 86 GT Last week from Indy  that monkeyman is buying this weekend!  <P>Total fieros hauled with this U-Haul dolly to date is well over 100 and counting! <P>I just had to jump in here on this one! sorry!!<BR>FD<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||1
